I've never understood why people are so anal about having free action
in the endgame.  There's a misconception that free action is the only
way to defend against priest paralysis attacks.  Magic resistance does
the SAME thing in this regard.  The only thing free action would
prevent against is the instance of a thrown potion of paralysis,
which, at least in my experience, is not very common.

The only case where free action is necessary in the entire endgame, I
think, is when all of the following are true:
1. On the Astral Plane, a priest or other monster is actually
generated with a potion of paralysis. (which is rare)
2. You are standing next to Pestilence or Famine.  (also rare, since
most priests will throw the potion at you right away, before you get
close to them)
3. The potion is thrown and hits you directly.  (not too rare, but
you're usually in the middle of a crowd)
4. The paralysis lasts long enough for them to kill you through
sickness or starvation.  According to the spoilers, you would be
paralyzed for 1-5 rounds in this case, and I'm pretty sure you could
take at least 2 rounds from either Pestilence or Famine without dying.
 
So, I think the chance of dying due to a lack of free action is pretty
small... and it probably has less of a net effect on ascension
probability than, say, a ring of increase damage or regeneration.
 
Admittedly, if you have a bad AC and/or no healing potions, then being
paralyzed in the middle of a crowd of angels and priests is dangerous
too, but I think this isn't normally the case considering how much
people generally prepare for the endgame.

